Privacy Policy
Last updated: June 29, 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how LIFT-COMPLEX DS, OOO ("Company", "we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, stores, and discloses information when you use the LKDS Alert mobile application (the "Application").
The Application is intended to register a mobile device for push notifications and to display alert messages received from the Company's server. The Application does not provide public profiles, public message boards, advertising features, or user-generated public content.

1. Company Information
Company: LIFT-COMPLEX DS, OOO
Address: Vostochnaya St, 25, Krasnoobsk, Novosibirsk Oblast, 630501, Russia
Contact email: aaa@lkds.ru

2. Information We Collect
The Application collects and processes only the information needed to register the device, deliver push notifications, and display alert messages.
2.1 Device Registration Data
Firebase Cloud Messaging token (FCM token): a technical token used to deliver push notifications to your device.
Device platform: whether the device is Android or iOS.
User ID: a server-generated identifier returned by the Company's server after device registration.
2.2 Alert Message Data
Alert ID: a technical identifier of an alert message.
Message content: the text of the alert message delivered by the Company's server and displayed in the Application.
2.3 Technical Connection Data
When the Application communicates with the Company's server, technical data may be processed automatically, including IP address, request time, server response status, and other technical data required for security, troubleshooting, and service operation.
2.4 Data Stored on the Device
The Application stores the server-generated User ID and the FCM token locally on the device to avoid repeating device registration on every launch. This local data is stored in the Application's local storage area and is used only for Application functionality.

3. Information We Do Not Collect
The Application does not intentionally collect the following categories of information:
name, email address, phone number, or postal address entered by the user;
precise or approximate location;
contacts, photos, videos, audio files, calendar data, or files from the device;
payment information or purchase history;
advertising identifiers for advertising or cross-app tracking;
browsing history or search history;
analytics data for marketing or behavioral profiling.

4. How We Use Information
We use the collected information for the following purposes:
to register your device for push notifications;
to deliver alert notifications to your device;
to load and display the list of alert messages assigned to your User ID;
to update the FCM token if it changes;
to maintain the security and reliability of the Application and server infrastructure;
to troubleshoot technical problems and respond to support requests.
We do not use the collected data for advertising, marketing profiling, or tracking users across apps or websites.

5. Push Notifications
The Application requests permission to send push notifications. You can enable or disable notifications at any time in your device operating system settings.
Push notifications may include alert message content. Depending on your device settings, notification content may be visible on the lock screen or in the notification center.

6. Service Providers and Third-Party Processing
The Application uses Firebase Cloud Messaging, a service provided by Google, to deliver push notifications. For this purpose, the Application obtains and sends an FCM token to the Company's server. Firebase may process technical identifiers and service data, such as Firebase installation IDs, application identifiers, package names or bundle IDs, IP addresses, and operational service data, to provide and maintain the Firebase Cloud Messaging service.
On iOS devices, Apple Push Notification service (APNs) may be used by the operating system and Firebase Cloud Messaging to deliver notifications.
The Company does not sell your personal data and does not share it with advertising networks or data brokers.

7. Data Transfers
The Application communicates with the Company's backend server at alert.lkds.net. Information may be processed at the Company's operating locations and by service providers used to deliver push notifications. Depending on the service provider infrastructure, this may involve processing in countries other than your country of residence.

8. Data Retention
We retain personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.
User ID and FCM token: retained while they are needed to provide push notifications and Application functionality.
Alert message data: retained as long as necessary to display alert messages and operate the alert service.
Technical server logs: may be retained for troubleshooting, security monitoring, and legal compliance for a limited period.
Uninstalling the Application may remove local data from your device, but it does not automatically delete data already stored on the Company's server. You may contact us to request deletion of data associated with your device or User ID.

9. Deletion and Access Requests
You may contact us to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal data associated with your device or User ID. We may need to retain certain information where required by law, for security reasons, or to resolve disputes.
The Application currently does not include an in-app account settings section for deleting server-side data. Requests should be sent to the contact email listed in this Privacy Policy.

10. Security
We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal data against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, or alteration. However, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
You should protect access to your device because alert notification content may be displayed by the operating system according to your notification settings.

11. Children's Privacy
The Application is not intended for children under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 16. If we become aware that we have collected personal data from a child under 16 without appropriate authorization, we will take steps to delete such information.

12. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make changes, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this document. Continued use of the Application after an updated Privacy Policy becomes available means that you acknowledge the updated terms.

13. Contact Us
If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or want to submit a privacy-related request, contact us by email:
aaa@lkds.ru
